---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const notes = (await getCollection("notes")).length;
const learn = (await getCollection("learn")).length;
---

<Base
  title="Bend Documentation"
  description="Concept-first documentation for HVM4 and Bend2: the main idea first, then depth."
  canonical="/"
  mdMirror="/index.md"
>
  <h1>Bend Documentation</h1>
  <p>
    Ordinary functional code already contains all the parallelism a machine
    could want. This documentation explains the runtime idea that makes it
    runnable (interaction nets), the machine built on it (HVM4), and Bend2 —
    the unreleased language combining automatic parallelism, dependent
    types, and synthesis. Main concept first, depth after. {notes} notes,
    {learn} hands-on pages, zero JavaScript required to read any of them.
  </p>
  <h2>Start here, by appetite</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Run code tonight</strong> — build HVM4 and watch one location
      hold two values:{" "}
      <a href="/learn/hvm-hands-on/">HVM4 hands-on</a>{" "}
      (runnable, outputs verified).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Understand the machine</strong> — how ten thousand workers
      rewrite one program without coordinating:{" "}
      <a href="/notes/interaction-nets/">Interaction nets, explained</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Follow Bend2</strong> — what it is and whether it's out:{" "}
      <a href="/notes/what-is-bend2/">What is Bend2?</a> ·{" "}
      <a href="/notes/release-status/">Release status</a> (currently: no).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Full reading order with tracks: <a href="/contents/">Contents</a>
    {" "}· machine-readable mirrors: <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="footdiv">
    <ul>
      <li></li>
      <li><a href="/contents/">Contents</a></li>
      <li><a class="nxtlink" href="/contents/">Contents</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p class="meta">Unofficial Bend documentation. Not affiliated with Higher Order Company.</p>
</Base>
